# 123 - aegis-scheme-alias v2 (r63 .deb desktop test finding, 2026-11-13)
# V1 registered the aegis:// alias scheme AND aliased WebUIConfigMap lookups
# (aegis://<host> resolved to chrome://<host> for every WebUI decision).
# The r63 desktop test proved that design CRASHES THE WHOLE BROWSER: a
# navigation to any WebUI-host aegis:// URL (aegis://version) commits with a
# process lock derived from the aegis:// origin while the WebUI machinery
# expects chrome:// - the commit-time WebUI check trips Chromium's
# IMMEDIATE_CRASH (ud2, SIGTRAP core verified). Non-WebUI aegis:// URLs are
# harmless (rejected safely), which is exactly why only WebUI hosts crashed.
#
# V2 keeps the alias scheme registration (standard + secure, so the omnibox
# parses aegis:// URLs) and DROPS the WebUIConfigMap aliasing entirely.
# Instead, a typed aegis:// URL is rewritten to chrome:// in the omnibox
# (AutocompleteInput::Parse) - the Aegis analogue of about:version ->
# chrome://version. Typed aegis://version, aegis://settings etc. therefore
# land on the real chrome:// WebUI pages; unrewritten aegis:// navigations
# (links, CDP) fail safely with an error page and never reach the WebUI
# commit path.

